A poor couple each secretly sell their most prized possession to buy the other a Christmas gift, leaving both gifts unusable but revealing their love as the wisest giving of all.

1. Poor Couples Christmas Longing  (passages 1-1)
    A poor young wife weeps because she has almost no money to buy her husband a worthy
    Christmas gift.
       -> Her poverty and love force her to consider what valuables they still have and to seek
       another way.
2. Two Treasures And Resolve  (passages 2-2)
    The couple own only two proud treasures, her long hair and his heirloom watch, and she
    rushes out determined to act.
       -> Her determination to honor his treasure pushes her to sacrifice her own treasure to
       pay for his gift.
3. Selling Hair For Chain  (passages 3-3)
    She sells her beautiful hair to buy a fine chain for his watch and returns home to curl what
    little hair remains.
       -> Her secret sacrifice and changed appearance create anxious suspense about how he will
       react when he arrives.
4. Anxious Reunion And Reassurance  (passages 4-5)
    He stares in stunned confusion at her short hair, reassures her his love is unchanged, and
    gives her a gift that swings her from joy to tears.
       -> His mysterious wrapped gift demands to be opened and explained, setting up the final
       reversal.
5. Useless Gifts Prove Wisest  (passages 6-6)
    They learn he sold his watch to buy her combs she can no longer use, just as her chain has
    no watch to hold, and their foolish sacrifice is praised as the wisest love.
